- **§12 / Module 12-C3 (Gate-code delivery truth + prod dispatcher · SMOKED 2026-10-28):** the "New gate verification code" modal said *SMS queued* and then *Console mode — no text is actually delivered*, and the same for email. Two causes, both fixed. **(1) Production had no dispatcher.** `infra/docker/docker-compose.prod.yml` omitted `background-worker` **and** `integration-gateway`, so `integration_outbox` was never polled and no process in prod could reach an SMS/email vendor — every notification sat `PENDING` (observed: 21 notifications / 31 outbox rows). Both services are now deployed internally (no host ports, `mem_limit` 160m/192m, reusing the multi-app `pssms-core-api:prod` image so no extra build is needed) and the worker points at `INTEGRATION_GATEWAY_URL=http://integration-gateway:4003`. Backlog drained on start: 62 outbox `PUBLISHED`, 47 notifications `SENT`, 3 WhatsApp `FAILED` (no adapter — by design). **(2) Transport was hard-coded.** `SMS_PROVIDER: console` was literal in the prod env anchor and no email/WhatsApp keys were passed through; all transport vars are now `${VAR:-default}` so `.env.prod` decides. **(3) The UI stopped over-claiming.** `enqueueVisitorGateCode` now returns `emailProvider` / `emailLive` / `emailRecipient` next to `smsProvider` / `smsLive` / `smsRecipient` (DTOS + api-client updated); the Call Centre modal renders “Email queued to …” with either “via <provider>” or an amber “console mode — nothing is delivered” warning instead of a flat “Code emailed to visitor”. **Smoke (local core-api :4101 + gateway :4003 + worker):** resend VIS-DEMO-006 → `delivery {sms:true, smsProvider:'fasthub', smsLive:true, smsRecipient:'+255712111006', email:true, emailProvider:'console', emailLive:false, emailRecipient:'rehema@clients.co.tz'}`; outbox poller dispatched → gateway logged `[SMS:fasthub] to=+255***006` + `SMS → fasthub SENT`; `notifications` rows both `SENT`; browser modal shows the new copy (code `JL2BN9HY`). Prod still needs `SMS_PROVIDER=fasthub` + `SMS_API_KEY`/`SMS_API_SECRET`/`SMS_SENDER_ID` (and `EMAIL_PROVIDER` + `EMAIL_API_URL` for real mail) in `infra/docker/.env.prod`, plus rebuilds of `core-api` + `admin-web` for the new fields/UI. Deferred: real Meta WhatsApp API, delivery-receipt callbacks, per-org credentials.
- **§4 / Module 5-M2 (Portal session persistence: silent refresh everywhere · SMOKED 2026-10-28):** every portal page that called the core API with a **hand-rolled `fetch`** showed a bare `Unauthorized` (or raw JSON envelope) banner once the 15-minute access token aged out, even though a refresh token was still on the device — observed on admin `/hr/b2b-requests` and the whole parking portal. **Root cause:** `frontend/packages/api-client` had ~15 copy-pasted refresh implementations and six modules with **none** (`recruitment-b2b`, `supplier`, `visitor-contractor`, `visitor-consultant`, `visitor-provider`, plus the public `visitor` helper), and `supplier.ts` still threw `new Error(await res.text())` (raw JSON in the vendor portal). **Fix:** new `packages/api-client/src/session.ts` — `createSessionFetch({ key, getAccessToken, getRefreshToken, setTokens, clearSession, loginPath })` gives one bearer fetch with a single-flight `POST /auth/refresh` + retry on the first 401, the bodyless-mutation `{}` trick, and a `?expired=1` redirect when the refresh token itself is rejected. Migrated all six modules onto it; `@pssms/auth` gained the missing `supplierAuth` refresh cookie (`pssms_supplier_refresh` — supplier login never stored a refresh token before) plus `getSupplier/P…RefreshToken` + `set…Tokens` for supplier/partner/contractor/consultant/provider. Supplier login now persists `result.tokens.refreshToken`, and the admin/supplier/partner/contractor/consultant/provider login screens render a friendly “Your session expired. Sign in again to continue.” banner for `?expired=1` (admin also keeps `?error=`). **Smoke (prod web.hisgc.co.tz / supplier. / visitor. / recruitment.hisgc.co.tz, rebuilt images):** admin — corrupt `pssms_admin_token` → `/hr/b2b-requests` silently refreshes, partner billing + GSR-00001 render, no banner; delete/corrupt the refresh token → redirect `/login?expired=1` with the amber notice. supplier — corrupt token → `/submissions` silently refreshes and lists SINV-00001/QT-00001. contractor — corrupt token → `/contractor` refreshes and renders the appointment form. partner — corrupt token → `/partner/requests` refreshes (JWT re-issued with `b2bPartnerId`). **Data repair:** `partner@demo-security.co.tz` logged in to `404 B2B partner not found` because its `b2b_partner_id` pointed at a deleted seed row — re-inserted `OSC-DEMO` (`71bd442e…`) so the documented demo partner works; `thomas@hisgc.co.tz` still points at a deleted `OSC-WATUCRED-N777` partner (left untouched, staff email self-registered as a partner). Deferred: consolidating the remaining duplicated `tryRefresh` blocks (admin/finance/hr/ess/loans/compliance/developer/documents/assets/branch-ops/customer/recruitment/parking already work) onto `createSessionFetch`; refresh-token rotation/revocation (backend `refresh` is stateless, so a stolen refresh JWT stays valid until it expires).
